# taf.ue.proxy.mngr

[![Documentation](https://docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/projects/taf-ue-proxy-mngr/badge/)][1]
[![Requirements](https://taf.wrgitlab-pages.int.net.nokia.com/miscellaneous/static-badges/requirements.svg)](requirements/base.txt)
[![build status](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/abstract_library/taf.ue.proxy.mngr/badges/main/pipeline.svg)][2]
[![coverage report](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/abstract_library/taf.ue.proxy.mngr/badges/main/coverage.svg)][2]
[![latest release](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/abstract_library/taf.ue.proxy.mngr/-/badges/release.svg)][3]

UE proxy manager  (HTTPS/HTTP microservice) running at UE PC

## Supported Python versions

Library should work properly with Python versions specified within
`python_requires` option in [setup.py](setup.py).

## Installation

Generic library installation process is described in [TAF user guide][4].

## starting server
You can check available options via:
```bash
python taf.ue.proxy/taf/ue/proxy/mngr/run_ue_proxy_mngr.py --help
```

## updating requirements/base.txt
Remember to update `dependencies.py3.lock` file each time you change `requirements/base.txt` via:
```bash
pip-compile --no-emit-find-links --no-emit-index-url --no-emit-trusted-host --output-file=dependencies.py3.lock requirements/base.txt
```

## vendoring
Vendored packages source: 'https://wrgitlab.ext.net.nokia.com/TAF/abstract_library/taf.ue.proxy'  
details in: `taf.ue.proxy.mngr/taf/ue/proxy/mngr/_vendor/ue_proxy/__version__.py`

## versioning
```plantuml
participant "taf.ue.*" as plugin
participant taf.ue.proxy_mng as mng
participant taf.ue.proxy as proxy
participant artifactory as art

autonumber

activate mng
plugin -> mng: /api/require_proxy_service(\nue_type,\nmin_required_proxy_ver,\nmin_required_access_ver,\nOptional: required_proxy_port)

alt if required versions of taf.ue.proxy and taf.ue.proxy.access.* available

note left of mng
major.minor.patch

major numbers are equal 
and minor.patch numbers are equal or greater
end note

mng -> proxy: run_ue_proxy
activate proxy
mng -> plugin: host, port
plugin --> proxy: e.g. require_ue()
proxy --> plugin:
deactivate proxy

else else

alt try download required versions

mng -> art: download required versions
mng -> proxy: run_ue_proxy
activate proxy
mng -> plugin: host, port
plugin --> proxy: e.g. require_ue()
proxy --> plugin:
deactivate proxy

else if fails
mng -> plugin: RequiredVersionNotAvailableException()

end
end
```

